# Ardyn, the Usurper makes a token copy of Clone from Bot2's graveyard ("except it's a 5/5 black Demon"). The token has
# Clone's ability, so it may enter as a copy of a creature (CR 707.9): it copies Outland Liberator, a copy effect over it
# that overwrites the Demon exception (CR 707.2) - a 2/2 green Human Werewolf with daybound. A token created with its own
# characteristics that enters as a copy of a double-faced permanent by a replacement effect is no double-faced token
# (CR 707.8a, its last sentence), so when night comes (CR 731.2) the Liberator card transforms and the token stays an
# Outland Liberator, front face up (CR 701.27c).
#
# Turn 1: Black Lotus and every Mox cast Ardyn ({5}{B}{B}{B}). Bot2 draws Clone on turn 2 and discards it to hand size.
# Turn 3: Outland Liberator from Mox Emerald and Mox Jet (it becomes day, CR 702.145d); at the beginning of combat
# Starscourge exiles the Clone and makes the token, which copies the Liberator. Bot2 casts nothing on turn 4, so turn 5 is
# night.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Ardyn, the Usurper
Outland Liberator
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x7
Clone
Swamp x12

[Actions]
